.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Vt OSSL_ENCODER
is a method for encoders, which know how to encode an object of some
kind to a encoded form, such as PEM, DER, or even human readable text.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_fetch
looks for an algorithm within the provider that has been loaded into the
.Vt OSSL_LIB_CTX
given by
.Fa ctx ,
having the name given by
.Fa name
and the properties given by
.Fa properties .
The
.Fa name
determines what type of object the fetched encoder method is expected to
be able to encode, and the properties are used to determine the expected
output type.
For known properties and the values they may have, please have a look in
.Xr provider-encoder 7 .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_up_ref
increments the reference count for the given
.Fa encoder .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_free
decrements the reference count for the given
.Fa encoder ,
and when the count reaches zero, frees it.
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_get0_provider
returns the provider of the given
.Fa encoder .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_get0_properties
returns the property definition associated with the given
.Fa encoder .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_is_a
checks if
.Fa encoder
is an implementation of an algorithm that's identifiable with
.Fa name .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_get0_name
returns the name used to fetch the given
.Fa encoder .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_get0_description
returns a description of the
.Em loader ,
meant for display and human consumption.
The description is at the discretion of the
.Em loader
implementation.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_names_do_all
traverses all names for the given
.Fa encoder ,
and calls
.Em fn
with each name and
.Fa data
as arguments.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_do_all_provided
traverses all encoder implementations by all activated providers in the
library context
.Fa libctx ,
and for each of the implementations, calls
.Em fn
with the implementation method and
.Fa arg
as arguments.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_gettable_params
returns an
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array of parameter descriptors.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_get_params
attempts to get parameters specified with an
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array
.Em params .
Parameters that the implementation doesn't recognise should be ignored.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_fetch
returns a pointer to the key management implementation represented by an
OSSL_ENCODER object, or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_up_ref
returns 1 on success, or 0 on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_free
doesn't return any value.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_get0_provider
returns a pointer to a provider object, or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_get0_properties
returns a pointer to a property definition string, or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_is_a
returns 1 of
.Fa encoder
was identifiable, otherwise 0.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_get0_name
returns the algorithm name from the provided implementation for the
given
.Fa encoder .
Note that the
.Fa encoder
may have multiple synonyms associated with it.
In this case the first name from the algorithm definition is returned.
Ownership of the returned string is retained by the
.Fa encoder
object and should not be freed by the caller.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_get0_description
returns a pointer to a description, or NULL if there isn't one.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_ENCODER_names_do_all
returns 1 if the callback was called for all names.
A return value of 0 means that the callback was not called for any
names.
